===Displayed text and organization===
The following addon directives change how an addon is organised and displayed as text in various locations within the game (e.g., the [[AddOn List]], compartment, and tooltips). Their values may be coloured using [[UI escape sequences]] (e.g., <span class="apitype">|c########|r</span>).

Similar to the <span class="apialt">AllowLoadLocale</span> [[#Inline directives|inline directive]], these addon directives may also be [[Localization|localized]] by appending a hyphen and the locale code (e.g., <span class="apialt">Title-enUS</span>).
{{note|A non-localized fallback should always be specified ''before'' localized ones, otherwise they will be unused.}}

=====<span class="apialt">Title</span>=====
<div style="margin-left:2em">
Name displayed in the AddOn List.
<syntaxhighlight lang="wowtoc">
## Title: Waiting for Godot
## Title-frFR: En attendant Godot
</syntaxhighlight>
</div>

=====<span class="apialt">Notes</span>=====
<div style="margin-left:2em">
Tooltip displayed in the AddOn List.
<syntaxhighlight lang="wowtoc">
## Notes: This word is |cFFFF0000red|r
## Notes-itIT: La parola è |cFFFF0000rossa|r
</syntaxhighlight>
</div>

=====<span class="apialt">Category</span>=====
<div style="margin-left:2em">
Category name displayed in the AddOn List, displayed as a collapsible header entry.
It is '''strongly recommended''' that you stick to the translated category names found on the [[Addon Categories]] page. This will ensure that your addon is consistently located with other addons in the same category across all locales.
<syntaxhighlight lang="wowtoc">
## Category: This is a test
## Category-deDE: Dies ist ein Test
</syntaxhighlight>
</div>

=====<span class="apialt">Group</span>=====
<div style="margin-left:2em">
Addon used for grouping multiple addons together in the AddOn List.

* The value must be the name of the main addon.
* Grouped addons are displayed in the AddOn List as indented sub-lists. These lists cannot be collapsed, unlike Categories.
** Nested groups are not supported by the AddOn List.
* If no Group has been manually specified, the client will attempt to automatically deduce membership of a group.
** Installed addons will be scanned to locate pairs of addons where the base name of one addon is a complete prefix of another, and where any form of dependency relation exists between the two in either direction.

<syntaxhighlight lang="wowtoc">
## Group: FooAuras
</syntaxhighlight>
</div>

===Displayed icons===
The following addon directives change how an AddOn is displayed as an icon in various locations within the game (e.g., the AddOn List and compartment).

=====<span class="apialt">IconTexture</span>=====
<div style="margin-left:2em">
Path to a texture file to be shown as the icon for this addon in the AddOn List.
<syntaxhighlight lang="wowtoc">
## IconTexture: Interface\Icons\TEMP
</syntaxhighlight>
</div>

=====<span class="apialt">IconAtlas</span>=====
<div style="margin-left:2em">
Name of a texture atlas to be shown as the icon for this addon in the AddOn List. Has a lower priority than <span class="apialt">IconTexture</span> if both are set.
<syntaxhighlight lang="wowtoc">
## IconAtlas: TaskPOI-Icon
</syntaxhighlight>
</div>

===Addon compartment integration===
{{section|{{LatestPatchInfo|icon=}}{{forever-inline}}|'''This section concerns content related to {{g|{{API LatestExpansion}}}} and {{g|forever}}.'''}}
The following addon directives will control the registration of the addon into the [[Addon compartment|addon compartment]] dropdown accessible from the minimap.

====<span class="apialt">AddonCompartmentFunc</span>====
<div style="margin-left:2em">
Name of a global function to be executed when the entry for this addon has been clicked in the addon compartment.
{{note|This directive is '''required''' to show the addon in the addon compartment dropdown when using automatic registration.}}
<syntaxhighlight lang="wowtoc">
## AddonCompartmentFunc: MyAddon_OnAddonCompartmentClick
</syntaxhighlight>
</div>

====<span class="apialt">AddonCompartmentFuncOnEnter</span>====
<div style="margin-left:2em">
Name of a global function to be executed when the entry for this addon has been highlighted in the addon compartment dropdown.
<syntaxhighlight lang="wowtoc">
## AddonCompartmentFuncOnEnter: MyAddon_OnAddonCompartmentEnter
</syntaxhighlight>
</div>

====<span class="apialt">AddonCompartmentFuncOnLeave</span>====
<div style="margin-left:2em">
Name of a global function to be executed when the entry for this addon is no longer highlighted in the addon compartment dropdown.
<syntaxhighlight lang="wowtoc">
## AddonCompartmentFuncOnLeave: MyAddon_OnAddonCompartmentLeave
</syntaxhighlight>
</div>

=== Loading conditions ===
The following addon directives control when an addon loads, and any dependencies that must or may load first.

====<span class="apialt">LoadOnDemand</span>====
<div style="margin-left:2em">
Set to <span class="apitype">1</span> to delay loading until <code>{{api|C_AddOns.LoadAddOn}}</code> is called.
<syntaxhighlight lang="wowtoc">
## LoadOnDemand: 1
</syntaxhighlight>
</div>

====<span class="apialt">Dependencies</span>====
<div style="margin-left:2em">
Addons that must load first. Aliases include <span class="apialt">RequiredDeps</span> and any word beginning with <code>Dep</code>.
{{note|This directive may be specified multiple times, with later instances appending to the list.}}
<syntaxhighlight lang="wowtoc">
## Dependencies: someAddOn, someOtherAddOn
## Dep: yetAnotherAddOn
</syntaxhighlight>
</div>

====<span class="apialt">OptionalDeps</span>====
<div style="margin-left:2em">
Addons that must load first if available.
<syntaxhighlight lang="wowtoc">
## OptionalDeps: someAddOn, someOtherAddOn
</syntaxhighlight>
</div>

====<span class="apialt">LoadWith</span>====
<div style="margin-left:2em">
Addons that, once loaded, will trigger this one to load. Also causes this addon to behave as <span class="apialt">LoadOnDemand</span>.
{{note|This directive may be specified multiple times, with later instances appending to the list.}}
<syntaxhighlight lang="wowtoc">
## LoadWith: someAddOn, someOtherAddOn
</syntaxhighlight>
</div>

====<span class="apialt">LoadManagers</span>====
<div style="margin-left:2em">
Addons that, if present, will cause this one to behave as <span class="apialt">LoadOnDemand</span>. See [[AddonLoader]] for an example.
{{note|This directive may be specified multiple times, with later instances appending to the list.}}
<syntaxhighlight lang="wowtoc">
## LoadManagers: someAddOn, someOtherAddOn
</syntaxhighlight>
</div>

====<span class="apialt">AllowLoadGameType</span>====
<div style="margin-left:2em">
Restricts loading this addon to ''case-insensitive'' game types or thier families.
{{note|This addon directive may be specified multiple times, with later instances appending to the list.}}
<syntaxhighlight lang="wowtoc">
## AllowLoadGameType: standard, classic
</syntaxhighlight>
{{note|Some game modes may be restricted to disallow loading of third-party addons.}}
{{warning|1=If at least 1 game type is specified and none of the game types are recognized by the client, the condition will be satisfied. For this reason, you should additionally use <span class="apialt">ExcludeLoadGameType</span> to exclude game types that are not universally recognized yet.}}

{{Template:GameTypes}}
</div>

====<span class="apialt">ExcludeLoadGameType</span>====
<div style="margin-left:2em">
Similar to <span class="apialt">AllowLoadGameType</span>, but prevents loading this addon on specific game types or their families.
{{note|This addon directive may be specified multiple times, with later instances appending to the list.}}
<syntaxhighlight lang="wowtoc">
## ExcludeLoadGameType: vanilla, wrath
</syntaxhighlight>
</div>

====<span class="apialt">OnlyBetaAndPTR</span>====
<div style="margin-left:2em">
Set to <span class="apitype">1</span> if an addon should only be loadable in Beta or PTR clients.
<syntaxhighlight lang="wowtoc">
## OnlyBetaAndPTR: 1
</syntaxhighlight>
</div>

====<span class="apialt">DefaultState</span>====
<div style="margin-left:2em">
Set to <span class="apitype">disabled</span> to require the user to explicitly enable the addon in the [[AddOn List]].
<syntaxhighlight lang="wowtoc">
## DefaultState: disabled
</syntaxhighlight>
</div>

===Saved variables===
{{main|Saving variables between game sessions}}

====<span class="apialt">LoadSavedVariablesFirst</span>====
<div style="margin-left:2em">
Set to <span class="apitype">1</span> if SavedVariables file(s) should be loaded before all script files for this addon.
{{note|1=If this is set to <span class="apitype">1</span> it cannot be turned off later in the file.}}
<syntaxhighlight lang="wowtoc">
## LoadSavedVariablesFirst: 1
</syntaxhighlight>
</div>

====<span class="apialt">SavedVariables</span>====
<div style="margin-left:2em">
Global variables to be stored in and read from <code>WTF\[account]\SavedVariables\MyAddOn.lua</code>.
{{note|This addon directive may be specified multiple times, with later instances appending to the list.}}
<syntaxhighlight lang="wowtoc">
## SavedVariables: MyAddOnNameVariableFoo, MyAddOnNameVariableBar
</syntaxhighlight>
</div>

====<span class="apialt">SavedVariablesPerCharacter</span>====
<div style="margin-left:2em">
Global variables to be stored in and read from <code>WTF\[account]\[server]\[character]\SavedVariables\MyAddOn.lua</code>.
{{note|This directive may be specified multiple times, with later instances appending to the list.}}
<syntaxhighlight lang="wowtoc">
## SavedVariablesPerCharacter: MyAddOnNameCharacterVariableFoo, MyAddOnNameCharacterVariableBar
</syntaxhighlight>
</div>

===Metadata===
The following addon directives may be accessed using {{api|C_AddOns.GetAddOnMetadata}}.

====<span class="apialt">Author</span>====
<div style="margin-left:2em">
The addon author's name.
<syntaxhighlight lang="wowtoc">
## Author: My Name
</syntaxhighlight>
</div>

====<span class="apialt">Version</span>====
<div style="margin-left:2em">
The addon version, which will be shown in the tooltip in the [[AddOn List]].
{{note|Some automatic updating tools may prefer that this begins with a numeric version number.}}
<syntaxhighlight lang="wowtoc">
## Version: 1.0.0
</syntaxhighlight>
</div>

====<span class="apialt">X-___</span>====
<div style="margin-left:2em">
Any custom metadata prefixed by "X-", such as "X-Date", "X-Website" or "X-Feedback"
<syntaxhighlight lang="wowtoc">
## X-Website: https://github.com/MyUser/MyAddOn
</syntaxhighlight>
</div>

===Uncategorized===
====<span class="apialt">AllowAddOnTableAccess</span>====
<div style="margin-left:2em">
Set to <span class="apitype">1</span> to allow the retrieval of the [[Using the AddOn namespace|namespace table]] of this addon via {{api|t=a|C_AddOns.GetAddOnLocalTable}}.
{{note|1=If this is set to <span class="apitype">1</span>, and further instances of it will be ignored.}}
<syntaxhighlight lang="wowtoc">
## AllowAddOnTableAccess: 1
</syntaxhighlight>
</div>

===Restricted===
The following addon directives are inaccessible to third-party addons.

====<span class="apialt">AllowLoad</span>====
<div style="margin-left:2em">
Restricts loading this addon to the [[API IsOnGlueScreen|GlueXML]] environment, [[FrameXML]] environment, or both.

;<span class="apitype">Both</span>
:Allow this addon to load without restriction in all environments.
;<span class="apitype">Game</span>
:Only load this addon in the FrameXML environment.
;<span class="apitype">Glue</span>
:Only load this addon in the GlueXML environment.
</div>

====<span class="apialt">EscalateErrorDuringLoad</span>====
<div style="margin-left:2em">
Boolean addon directive that appears to have no effect in public clients.
</div>

====<span class="apialt">LoadFirst</span>====
<div style="margin-left:2em">
Set to <span class="apitype">1</span> if a secure addon is not permitted to be disabled and should be loaded before any other addons without this flag.
</div>

====<span class="apialt">SavedVariablesMachine</span>====
<div style="margin-left:2em">
List of global variable names to be persisted across all accounts on the same machine.
</div>

====<span class="apialt">UseSecureEnvironment</span>====
<div style="margin-left:2em">
Set to <span class="apitype">1</span> if all files present in an addon should be loaded into a private function environment.
</div>

==Inline directives==
TOC files support the inline use of a set of directives, which define the conditions under or behaviour with which their corresponding addon directive or file will apply. They use the syntax <syntaxhighlight lang="wowtoc" inline>[Directive]</syntaxhighlight> or <syntaxhighlight lang="wowtoc" inline>[Directive Value]</syntaxhighlight> with case insensitive values. Multiple inline directices can be used per line, and can appear anywhere in a line.
{{note|For reasons of compatibility, inline directives should generally only ever be used at the end of a line.}}

The following directives are supported inline:
;<span class="apialt">AllowLoad</span>
:Restricts the addon directive or file to in-game (<span class="apitype">Game</span>), glue screen (<span class="apitype">Glue</span>), or both (<span class="apitype">Both</span>) environments.
:{{note|Functionally inoperable for addons, as only Blizzard addons are loaded within the glue screen environment.}}
;<span class="apialt">AllowLoadGameType</span>
:Restricts the addon directive or file to one or multiple specific game types, delimited by commas.
:The possible values are the same as used by the [[#AllowLoadGameType|AllowLoadGameType directive]].
:{{warning|1=If at least 1 game type is specified and none of the game types are recognized by the client, the condition will still be satisfied. For this reason, you should additionally use <span class="apialt">ExcludeLoadGameType</span> inline to exclude game types that are not universally recognized yet.}}
;<span class="apialt">ExcludeLoadGameType</span>
:Similar to <code>[<span class="apialt">AllowLoadGameType</span> <span class="apitype">...</span>]</code>, but restricts the addon directive or file to the game type(s) not listed.
;<span class="apialt">AllowLoadTextLocale</span>
:Restricts the addon directive or file to one or more specific client text locales, delimited by commas.
:The possible values are the same as returned by {{api|t=a|GetLocale}}, eg. "enUS" and "frFR".
;<span class="apialt">AllowLoadEnvironment</span>
:Restricts the addon directive or file to the global (<span class="apitype">Global</span>) or secure (<span class="apitype">Secure</span>) environment.
:{{note|Functionally inoperable for addons, as only Blizzard addons are loaded within the secure environment.}}
;<span class="apialt">Bootstrap</span>
:Restricts the addon directive or file to the bootstrap process for <span class="apialt">LoadOnDemand</span> addons.
;<span class="apialt">LoadIntoEnvironment</span>
:Loads the file into the global (<span class="apitype">Global</span>) or secure (<span class="apitype">Secure</span>) environment.
:{{note|Functionally inoperable for addons, as only Blizzard code can be loaded into the secure environment.}}

Example:
{{#tag:syntaxhighlight|
## Interface: {{API LatestInterface}}
## Title: My Cool AddOn
## Title: My Cool AddOn in Classic [AllowLoadGameType classic]

# This will only be loaded on Standard (retail).
StandardOnly.lua [AllowLoadGameType standard]

# This will only be loaded on Camelot (forever).
ForeverOnly.lua [AllowLoadGameType camelot][ExcludeLoadGameType standard, classic]

# This will only be loaded in Vanilla or TBC.
VanillaOrTBC.lua [AllowLoadGameType vanilla, tbc]

# This will only be loaded under English or French client locales.
EnglishOrFrenchOnly.lua [AllowLoadTextLocale enUS, frFR]
|lang="wowtoc"}}

==Patch changes==
===Modern===
* {{Patch 12.1.7|note=
** Added <span class="apialt">RegionalTextLocale</span> variable.
** Prevented use of variables in addon directives.}}
* {{Patch 12.1.5|note=Added <span class="apitype">Standard</span> TOC suffix.}}
* {{Patch 12.1.0|note=Added <span class="apialt">Bootstrap</span> inline directive.}}
* {{Patch 12.0.7|note=Added inline directives and variables for addon directives.}}
* {{Patch 12.0.0|note=Added <span class="apialt">ExcludeLoadGameType</span> directive.}}
* {{Patch 11.2.0|note=Added the <span class="apialt">TextLocale</span> variable and <span class="apialt">AllowLoadTextLocale</span> directive.}}
* {{Patch 11.1.7|note=Added the <span class="apialt">AllowAddOnTableAccess</span> addon directive.}}
* {{Patch 11.1.5|note=
**Added variables for files.
**Added a subset of directives as inline directives for files.
**Added the <span class="apialt">LoadSavedVariablesFirst</span> addon directive.
**<span class="apialt">AllowLoadGameType</span> is now usable by insecure addons.}}
* {{Patch 11.1.0|note=Added the <span class="apialt">Category</span> and <span class="apialt">Group</span> addon directives.}}
* {{Patch 11.0.0|note=
**Added the restricted <span class="apialt">UseSecureEnvironment</span> addon directive.
**Removed the <span class="apialt">SuppressLocalTableRef</span> addon directive.}}
* {{Patch 10.2.7|note=
**Added support for comma-delimited <span class="apialt">Interface</span> versions.
**Added the restricted <span class="apialt">SuppressLocalTableRef</span> addon directive.
**Renamed <span class="apialt">AllowLoadByGameMode</span> and <span class="apialt">GuardedAddOn</span> directives to <span class="apialt">AllowLoadGameType</span> and <span class="apialt">LoadFirst</span>, respectively.}}
* {{Patch 10.2.6|note=Added the restricted <span class="apialt">AllowLoadByGameMode</span> addon directive.}}
* {{Patch 10.1.0|note=
**Added <span class="apialt">IconAtlas</span>, <span class="apialt">IconTexture</span>, and [[Addon compartment]] related addon directives.
**Added the restricted <span class="apialt">GuardedAddOn</span> addon directive.}}
* {{Patch 9.1.0|note=Multiple TOC files are now supported using a suffix to disambiguate Classic, BCC and Retail.<ref name="WoWUIBug#68">{{Ref web|author=Meo[[File:Inv g fishingbobber 05.png|12px]]rawr|url=https://github.com/Stanzilla/WoWUIBugs/issues/68#issuecomment-889431675|title=Multiple Interface Version Support|publisher=WoWUIBugs}}</ref>}}
* {{Patch 9.0.1|note=<code>[[MACRO reload|/reload]]</code> recognizes changes to TOC directives and entirely new files in the <code>Interface/AddOns/</code> directory tree.}}
* {{Patch 4.0.1|note=<code>[[MACRO reload|/reload]]</code> recognizes changes to the file order.}}
* {{Patch 2.1.0|note=Added the <span class="apialt">LoadManagers</span> addon directive.}}
* {{Patch 1.11.0|note=Added the <span class="apialt">Secure</span> addon directive.}}
* {{Patch 1.9.0|note=Added the <span class="apialt">LoadWith</span> addon directive.}}

